p('Related work. Ehrenborg-Readdy [ER2] develop the Tchebyshev transforms and an eigenvector construction that motivates [H]. Hetyei\'s earlier Tchebyshev posets [H1] and triangulations [H2], and the generalizations with Nevo [HN], provide the combinatorial background. The kernel failure here concerns Hetyei\'s second-kind interval transform, and does not refute the ER transform results. Its significance is modest and concrete: a finite exact counterexample to a structural conjecture, with a symmetric kernel direction already in degree five.')
